// bubbler profile: firefox
//
// Sound is `pulseaudio`: Firefox is a libpulse client (`libpulse` is in
// the Arch package's Depends) and reaches the server through
// $XDG_RUNTIME_DIR/pulse/native, which is what that grant binds.
// `pipewire` binds only pipewire-0, the native socket, and is what the
// screen-share portal hands frames over. Bare, either socket is playback
// only: nothing a page asks for through getUserMedia is reachable, with
// the policy drop-in installed; `lint` warns `audio-policy-missing`
// where it is not.
//   pulseaudio { microphone }
//     — the microphone a web meeting's getUserMedia call asks for.
//       Every microphone and line-in the session has becomes
//       reachable, and capture from them.
//
// `network` is the sandbox's own network namespace. Chromecast discovery
// is mDNS on the LAN and pasta does not bridge, so casting does not find
// anything; `network "host"` brings it back, together with every service
// on the host's loopback.
//
// Gecko has defaulted to Wayland since Firefox 121 and takes the display
// from the `wayland` grant, so no `env` node sets MOZ_ENABLE_WAYLAND;
// `env MOZ_ENABLE_WAYLAND="0"` goes back to Xwayland.
//
// `portals { screencast }` is the ScreenCast and Screenshot portals on
// top of the bundle's safe set: a file chooser, a link, a notification.
// The bare node grants none of them. Screen sharing needs `pipewire`
// too — the portal picks the source, PipeWire carries the frames.
//
// `dbus` is the proxied session bus. It is here because a portal call is
// a bus call and `portals` cannot work without one; the bare node opens
// no name of its own, and every rule the proxy carries comes from the
// bundles beside it.
//
// `dri` is the GPU. Without it Gecko composites in software, which
// renders every page and costs frame rate and battery on a video. Bare,
// so the sandbox gets the render nodes and not the card nodes. What bare
// `dri` binds anyway on the proprietary NVIDIA driver, whose EGL will not
// take a Wayland display without the primary node, `lint` notes.
//
// `home-share "Downloads" mode=rw` is where a download lands, and the
// only part of the real home this profile shares. Picking a file to
// upload goes the other way, through the portal file chooser, which
// needs no share at all.
//
// Bare by design. Add:
//   pipewire
//     — screen and window sharing: the portal picks the source and hands
//       the stream over PipeWire, so both grants are needed.
//   dbus {
//       own "org.mozilla.firefox.*"
//   }
//     — in place of the bare `dbus` node above, since one config carries
//       one `dbus` node: the remote-instance protocol, which a second
//       `firefox` reaches the running one through instead of starting
//       beside it.
//   notify
//     — desktop notifications a page asks for. Needs `dbus`.
//   mpris name="firefox.*"
//     — media keys and the desktop's player controls for a tab that is
//       playing. Needs `dbus`.
//   app-runtime "org.keepassxc.KeePassXC"
//     — KeePassXC browser integration. Grant the same id in the
//       `keepassxc` instance (it lists the line in its own header).
//       Read-only is enough: this side only connects to the socket
//       KeePassXC serves.
wayland
dri
pulseaudio
network
dbus
portals {
    screencast
}
home-share "Downloads" mode=rw
command "firefox"
